.env*
# Secrets - never commit admin credentials
/docs/ADMIN_CREDENTIALS.txt

# Local integrity/quarantine state. This is machine-local output written by the
# price-integrity tooling, not part of the application - the sibling entries
# above cover cache/sessions/views/logs but not the framework root, so
# `git add -A` would otherwise sweep it in.
/storage/framework/*.json

# Scraped component imagery: 2,603 JPEGs totalling ~200 MB. These are downloaded
# product photos, not source. The components table already carries an image_url
# column, so the images belong on a CDN/object store with the URL in the
# database; committing them would add 200 MB of permanent history to the repo
# and slow or break every Vercel build.
/public/img/components/

# CC0 PBR textures are fetched by scripts/fetch-pbr-textures.php, not committed.
# 7.8MB of binaries in git is a bad trade for files that are reproducible from
# pinned Poly Haven asset names. manifest.json IS committed, so the material slots
# and their licences stay reviewable in code.
public/textures/pbr/*.jpg

# --- Pre-refresh catalogue backups (2026-10-06) ----------------------------
# 13.6MB of .bak snapshots taken before the case/cooler/cpu/gpu/ram refresh.
# The live scraped/*.json files are already tracked, so these are redundant
# rollback copies that only ever grow. The refresh is reproducible from
# scripts/start-catalogue-refresh.ps1, so the backups are not history.
database/scraped/*.bak

# --- Runtime database snapshots (2026-10-09) ---------------------------------
# scripts/genie-backfill-psu-efficiency.php dumps every specs object it is about
# to change here BEFORE writing, giving a reversible rollback point. These are
# production data snapshots, never code, and must never be swept into a commit.
scripts/backups/

# --- Scratch files ---------------------------------------------------------
# One-off batch generators written to be run and thrown away. A file named
# tmp-*.php has never once been the thing we wanted to keep.
database/scraped/tmp-*.php
scripts/tmp-*.php

# --- Runtime state, not source ---------------------------------------------
# mesh-spec-trust.json is written at runtime by the 3D trust gate. Committing
# it would freeze a machine-specific verdict into the repo.
storage/app/

# Batch sweep output: empty stub files and logs from a one-off run.
database/scraped/prod-batches/

# Vite hot-reload marker. Laravel's @vite directive reads this file and, if it
# exists, replaces every asset URL with the dev server. A stale public/hot
# containing http://127.0.0.1:5173 was uploaded by `vercel --prod` on
# 2026-10-07 and the whole site rendered as unstyled text because no CSS or JS
# could load. It is untracked, which is exactly why it shipped: the deploy
# uploads the working directory, not just tracked files. Never commit, and
# scripts/deploy.ps1 now fails the build if it is present.
public/hot
